## 2026-09-22 21:20 IST — Approved Implementation & Runtime Acceptance: Partially-Published Card Recovery Defect

### Why this work was requested
- User requested investigation and implementation of a fix for an interrupted 3-property batch publish incident (`draft-single-mucr34e3-rf2nx`).
- Batch contained 3 properties: (1) Viman Nagar, (2) Kali Nagar, (3) Mhow.
- Network was disconnected during publishing. When reconnected:
  - Backend had fully published #73 (Viman, 3 media) and #74 (Kali, 4 media).
  - Listing #75 (Mhow) was created in PostgreSQL at the start of the batch, but its 3 media files remained pending in B2 draft staging.
  - The UI summary displayed "2 of 3 properties published" and "1 property remaining", but the remaining review card for Mhow displayed a blue "Published" badge and the publish button was disabled ("Confirm remaining property").
- Diagnosis proved backend state was coherent, and the defect was a semantic overload of `publishedId` on the frontend.

### Semantic Contract Defined
- `publishedId`: Authoritative listing identity already exists for this card (`LISTING_CREATED_MEDIA_PENDING`). It does NOT mean the card has completed publication.
- `completedListings`: Authoritative completion. A card is fully published ONLY when authoritative reconciliation places it in `completedListings`.
- A card remaining in `stagedCards` with `publishedId != null` is NOT fully published, MUST display a recovery badge ("Media Pending", not "Published"), and MUST be resumable.
- Readiness: `readyToPublishCount` must include valid staged cards with `publishedId`.
- Resumption: Resuming a card with `publishedId` must target the existing listing ID directly and make NO listing-creation requests.

