## 2026-09-22 14:30 IST — Approved Implementation: B2 Draft Media Transient Error Hardening

### Why this work was requested
- User requested implementation of the approved exception hardening for draft media staging against Backblaze B2.
- During physical network interruption testing, transient `SocketException: Unexpected end of file from server` occurred and was classified as generic HTTP 500.
- Approved Phase 1 design implemented with explicit requirement: transient storage/network interruptions return **HTTP 503 SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE** (NOT HTTP 502 Bad Gateway) with safe customer-facing error messages, while non-transient storage or credential misconfigurations map to HTTP 500 INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR.
- Strict scope constraints: No frontend changes, no additional retry layer (AWS SDK retries preserved), no modification to publishing, batch reconciliation, Cloudinary pipeline, FailedUploadService, schema, Flyway migrations, database data, or B2/Cloudinary data.

### Root Cause
- Draft media staging exceptions were previously caught generically in `PropertyDraftService` and wrapped into `IllegalStateException("Failed to store temporary draft media. Please try again.")`, reaching the fallback `Exception.class` handler in `GlobalExceptionHandler` which returned HTTP 500 Internal Server Error without distinguishing temporary transport/network interruptions from permanent configuration errors.

### Files Created
- `backend/src/main/java/com/indore/pathome/spaces/exception/MediaStagingException.java` [NEW]:
  - Dedicated exception carrying `boolean transientFailure`, `String safeReason`, `String stagingKey`, and internal `diagnostic` message with cause.

### Files Modified
- `backend/src/main/java/com/indore/pathome/spaces/service/S3MediaStagingService.java`:
  - Added `isTransientFailure(Throwable t)`: Classifies `SocketException`, `SocketTimeoutException`, `ConnectException`, `UnknownHostException`, `ApiCallTimeoutException`, `ApiCallAttemptTimeoutException`, `S3Exception` status codes 429, 500, 502, 503, 504, and network I/O errors (broken pipe, connection reset, EOF) as transient. Classifies permission/authorization (e.g. S3 403 Forbidden) and invalid request errors as non-transient.
  - Updated `stage()` to catch storage errors, classify via `isTransientFailure()`, log transient failures at `WARN` and non-transient failures at `ERROR` with diagnostic context, and throw `MediaStagingException`.
- `backend/src/main/java/com/indore/pathome/spaces/service/PropertyDraftService.java`:
  - Updated `stageDraftMedia()` to explicitly catch and rethrow `MediaStagingException` without wrapping in `IllegalStateException`, preserving transaction and persistence behavior.
- `backend/src/main/java/com/indore/pathome/spaces/exception/GlobalExceptionHandler.java`:
  - Added dedicated `@ExceptionHandler(MediaStagingException.class)`.
  - Transient failures return `HttpStatus.SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE` (503) with safe message `"Media staging was temporarily interrupted. Please try uploading the file again."` and `WARN` logging.
  - Non-transient failures return `HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR` (500) with safe message `"Draft media storage is currently unavailable. Please try again later."` and `ERROR` logging.
  - Enforced zero information leakage: internal diagnostic details, stack traces, AWS request IDs, and credentials are kept server-side only.
- `backend/src/test/java/com/indore/pathome/spaces/exception/GlobalExceptionHandlerTest.java`:
  - Added tests verifying HTTP 503 for transient failures, HTTP 500 for non-transient failures, safe error messages, and zero leak of internal diagnostics.
- `backend/src/test/java/com/indore/pathome/spaces/service/MediaStagingServiceTest.java`:
  - Added tests for `SocketException` (transient -> true), `S3Exception` 503 (transient -> true), `S3Exception` 403 (transient -> false), and `ApiCallTimeoutException` (transient -> true).
- `backend/src/test/java/com/indore/pathome/spaces/service/PropertyDraftServiceTest.java`:
  - Added test verifying `stageDraftMedia()` propagates `MediaStagingException` cleanly without wrapping in `IllegalStateException`.

### Summary of Outcome
- Transient B2/network staging failures are cleanly classified as HTTP 503 SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE with WARN logging.
- Non-transient staging failures are classified as HTTP 500 INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR with ERROR logging.
- Zero API information leakage verified: raw AWS messages, bucket secrets, and endpoint details are excluded from responses.
- No frontend changes made (existing client architecture safely handles non-2xx responses by marking media as failed and isolating it from autosave).
- No additional application retry layer added (preserves standard AWS SDK retry semantics).
- B2 object key strategy (`drafts/{adminId}/{draftId}/{mediaId}_{safeFilename}`), UNIQUE(media_id), and idempotency behavior remain completely preserved.

